paper/src/reach26-arXiv.tex:645:Let $B\subseteq A$ be the unit square incident to the lower-left corner of $A$. Since all anchors have integer coordinates, every empty square containing $B$ is also contained in $A$.
paper/src/reach26-arXiv.tex:646:If a pair $(A,s)$ has property~\ref{case1}, apart from $A$, no such empty square has a corner at an undecided anchor and, hence, $B$ cannot be covered.
paper/src/reach26-arXiv.tex:647:If a pair $(A,s)$ has property~\ref{case2}, $B$ must be covered by a square anchored at its upper-left corner, which is undecided by hypothesis.
